  "description": "fetchproxy protocol 4 room<->extension frame vectors: bridge-role, bridge-serve, room-ping, room-pong. Written from the spec (mcp-host docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-05-multi-browser-bridge-design.md §5.8) and the plan's F1 section, independently of the implementation. `valid` frames must be accepted by validateFrame and come back equal; `invalid` frames must be refused. `literals` are the only texts a room-ping / room-pong may be on the wire; `invalidTexts` are other serialisations that must be refused. `accepts` names, per frame type, the entry the extension's hello must list for that frame to cross the link. Every transcription (mcp-host's room) is tested against this file.",
